4-602.13 The following nonfood contact surfaces were observed to be soiled:
A) storage freezer - bottom inside (debris);
B) counter under tea maker (dust/debris);
C) cookie oven - bottom inside (carbon/food debris);
D) oven - surface under cookie oven (food debris); and
E) inside mop bucket (general buildup) 
Cleaning frequency was discussed. Nonfood contact surfaces shall be cleaned at a frequency necessary to eliminate buildup of grease, food splash and general debris.
